Subject: [PATCH 29/38] GL overlay: margin extend actually works now
 (off-by-half-pixel probe)

The clamp-extend sampled exactly the nominal margin-edge column - the
one column that is NEVER covered, because quad vertices carry a +0.5
coarse offset so hardware coverage starts ~2 fine px inside the edge.
It silently filled nothing. The probe now walks a short inward run
(and covers the 8 px skirt, killing the boundary hairline). Regenerated
from gpu/renderer.py; exact mode re-verified 100.0000% (incl. the new
offroadc showcase capture that exposed the bug).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QABHMhAzD8GxaNT8zBVLho
