From 5d0e2f95acee02701803a331d7f78691d51ce0eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: d-b-c-e <anthony.mason1@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 14:37:41 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 38/38] zeus2: skip MAME's CPU rasterization when the live
 overlay renders

With MIDZ_GL the game was rendered TWICE: our GL renderer draws every quad,
and MAME's CPU rasterizer drew them all again into the never-displayed
frameColor. When live, fill a LOCAL raster-state struct for the emit path
(never touching poly_manager's object ring) and skip render_triangle_fan.
Fast clears / frame writes still hit frameColor directly and are replayed
in GL, so 2D screens are unaffected; offline capture (oracle) still
rasterizes.

Measured under identical ambient load minutes apart: crusnexo 94.3% ->
99.68/99.76/99.80% across three runs - the overlay's emu-thread cost is
gone, matching crusnusa (99.81%) on the same box. (An earlier attempt at
this measured 80-86% and was reverted - those runs were polluted by
Defender scans of freshly built exes; the discriminating USA-vs-Exotica
pair exposed the real headroom picture.)

